#: ../../source/developers/apps/index.rst:7
msgid "These pages explain how SEPAL decides which app code to run and how that code reaches the platform — useful when you want to add an app, ship a new version of an existing one, or package a reusable environment for a notebook or workflow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/apps/index.rst:14
msgid "The set of apps SEPAL runs is curated in the `dfguerrerom/sepal-apps-catalog <https://github.com/dfguerrerom/sepal-apps-catalog>`__ repository. Getting an app onto SEPAL — or updating one — means opening a pull request there. For docker apps, the catalog also pins the *exact commit* SEPAL will run; for jupyter apps, the catalog records the ``branch`` and SEPAL still runs the tip of that branch. The pages below walk through both flows."
msgstr ""

